  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130550",
      "title": "\"final\" & \"const\" - Special Kinds Of \"Variables\"",
      "lectureOrder": 42,
      "videoOrder": 39,
      "sourceHash": "730575c29e0b33197ee8e1b64d442a174d64cf8b56af6180423d916ce1237873",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "Now, there is more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "you should know about variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "For example, you sometimes have variables that never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "Of course, technically, it's called variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 14.169,
          "en": "because the value is variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.169,
          "end": 17.19,
          "en": "but in the end, it's all about having data containers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.19,
          "end": 20.039,
          "en": "and those data containers could also be set once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.039,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "and never changed thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 25.902,
          "en": "For example, here, I never assign new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.902,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "to start and endAlignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "And if you know that this is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 35.475,
          "en": "it's recommended that you use final instead of var.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.475,
          "end": 37.615,
          "en": "Final is a never built-in keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.615,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "which simply means that this data container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 43.92,
          "en": "will never receive a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.92,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "And whilst you could, of course, stick to var,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 49.939,
          "en": "it's always a good practice to be as restrictive as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.939,
          "end": 54.12,
          "en": "so that you never accidentally reassign a value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "Of course, you are the only one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "working on this project here probably,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "but in bigger teams",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "with multiple developers working on the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.569,
          "en": "you wanna be as restrictive as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.569,
          "end": 66.24,
          "en": "to make sure that some colleague of yours",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 67.841,
          "en": "is not accidentally overriding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.841,
          "end": 69.839,
          "en": "one of your variable values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.839,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "somewhere else in the overall project code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "That's why the final keyword exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.28999999999999,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "Now, here, I'm of course, getting some blue squiggly lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "that I should use const instead of final in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 85.47800000000001,
          "en": "And indeed, that's another usage of const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.47800000000001,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "which we haven't seen up to this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 91.593,
          "en": "You can create so-called constant variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.593,
          "end": 95.10300000000001,
          "en": "or constant data containers, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.97,
          "end": 98.035,
          "en": "It's almost the same as final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.035,
          "end": 100.38,
          "en": "because const also makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.38,
          "end": 103.05199999999999,
          "en": "that you can't reassign those variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.05199999999999,
          "end": 104.417,
          "en": "But unlike final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.417,
          "end": 107.88300000000001,
          "en": "it provides some extra information to Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "When using const here in front of a variable name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "so on the left side of the equals sign in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "you're telling Dart that the value that's stored in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 121.47,
          "en": "is a so-called compile-time constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "which means it's simply locked in at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 126.48,
          "en": "this code is compiled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.48,
          "end": 128.97,
          "en": "Now, that's not necessarily always the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.97,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "You could, for example, also have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 134.52100000000002,
          "en": "where you're maybe calling a function, getAlignment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.52100000000002,
          "end": 136.74,
          "en": "which doesn't exist in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.74,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "but which could exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "and which then behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "could dynamically calculate the desired alignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 145.68,
          "en": "You could definitely have something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.68,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "and if that's the case, that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "means that this function must be executed when the app runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 156.63,
          "en": "to get the actual alignment value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 158.94,
          "en": "In that case, it might still be final.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 161.56900000000002,
          "en": "You don't reassign the variable thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.56900000000002,
          "end": 164.01,
          "en": "but it's not compile-time constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.01,
          "end": 167.46,
          "en": "because the value that might be returned by get alignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.46,
          "end": 169.44,
          "en": "is not known at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "when this code is compiled yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 174.603,
          "en": "Instead, it's only known once the code executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "And here that's different for Alignment.topLeft;.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 181.064,
          "en": "This indeed is locked in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.064,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "at the point of time this code is compiled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 185.923,
          "en": "topLeft is clearly defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.923,
          "end": 188.52,
          "en": "to the top left corner of the device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.52,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "so to certain X and Y coordinate values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "And therefore, you can use const to tell Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 197.803,
          "en": "that this is not dynamically derived at runtime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.803,
          "end": 201.84,
          "en": "but can be locked in and set at compilation time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.84,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "And this is another potential performance improvement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 207.108,
          "en": "because if some value can be locked in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.108,
          "end": 210.03,
          "en": "at the point of time the code is compiled,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.03,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "this code doesn't have to execute when the app executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 214.88,
          "en": "Instead, this locked in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 214.88,
          "end": 218.445,
          "en": "and internally saved value can be used by Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 218.445,
          "end": 222,
          "en": "when this code is about to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "So, it's some internal performance optimization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "and therefore here, when defining variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 230.16,
          "en": "you should also use const instead of final",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.16,
          "end": 232.17000000000002,
          "en": "whenever it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 236.16,
          "en": "So, whenever you have such a compile-time constant value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 239.562,
          "en": "And just as before, the code Editor will simply tell you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 239.562,
          "end": 242.55,
          "en": "when you have such an opportunity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "By the way, with that set to const,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 246.36,
          "en": "you can also re-add const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 246.36,
          "end": 249.3,
          "en": "down there in front of BoxDecoration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 252.687,
          "en": "because now that this is const instead of var,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 252.687,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "you guarantee that it will never be reassigned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 258.315,
          "en": "and therefore, you can use const here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 258.315,
          "end": 262.344,
          "en": "because this code is now no longer potentially variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.344,
          "end": 265.47,
          "en": "because it can't be set in any other place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.47,
          "end": 267.3,
          "en": "It can only be set once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 268.56,
          "en": "and therefore, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 268.56,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "we can unlock this potential optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 274.26,
          "en": "of the BoxDecoration object again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.26,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "And in case this is all not 100% clear just yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 281.571,
          "en": "you will see variables and final values and constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 281.571,
          "end": 284.64,
          "en": "over and over again throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 284.64,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "but it is important to be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 288.27,
          "en": "of these concepts right now already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 288.27,
          "end": 291.423,
          "en": "because we'll use more variables in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
